[E0350] Error: an owned closure cannot capture `items`, a reference
    ╭─[ err/105_owned_closures/main.wip:11:16 ]
    │
 11 │     own (i) => items[i]             // a reference does not outlive the call
    │                ──┬──  
    │                  ╰──── captured here
    │ 
    │ Help: pass it to the closure as a parameter, or capture what it refers to by value
    │ 
    │ Note: an owned closure outlives the call that made it, and a reference does not
────╯
[E0304] Error: cannot assign to `total`, which this closure captured
    ╭─[ err/105_owned_closures/main.wip:16:9 ]
    │
 16 │         total += x
    │         ──┬──  
    │           ╰──── captured by value
    │ 
    │ Help: take what changes as a parameter of the closure
    │ 
    │ Note: an owned closure holds what it captured and reads it; whether it may change it is left for later
────╯
[E0301] Error: an owned closure is written here, and `(i64) => i64` is expected
    ╭─[ err/105_owned_closures/main.wip:21:29 ]
    │
 21 │ fn intoPlain(): i64 = plain(own (x) => x + 1, 2)
    │                             ────────┬───────  
    │                                     ╰───────── an owned closure
    │ 
    │ Help: leave out `own`, so the lambda is lent for the call
    │ 
    │ Note: `own (x) => …` allocates an environment that holds what it captured
────╯
